Formula:
For interval [min, max] with resolution ε (for integers, ε = 1):
• Lower boundary values: {min - ε, min} → {min - 1 (invalid), min (valid)}
• Upper boundary values: {max, max + ε} → {max (valid), max + 1 (invalid)}
• Total test values = 4 values: {min - 1, min, max, max + 1}

Example for range [1, 10]:
Values = {0, 1, 10, 11}
• Valid: 1, 10
• Invalid: 0, 11

Formula:
Tests 3 values per boundary:
• Lower boundary: {min - ε, min, min + ε}
• Upper boundary: {max - ε, max, max + ε}
• Total test values = 6 values: {min - ε, min, min + ε, max - ε, max, max + ε}

Example for integer range [10, 50] (ε = 1):
Values = {9, 10, 11, 49, 50, 51}
• Valid: 10, 11, 49, 50
• Invalid: 9, 51
